    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Isaac Paredes** (66.57) and **Brice Turang** (63.14) headline our offensive output. **Isaac Paredes** earns top marks due to a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez; the combination of a +16% SP skill adjustment and a significant platoon edge (+9%) makes him our anchor. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** remains a high-floor start despite a challenging encounter with George Kirby. His score is bolstered by the premium slot at the top of the order (+10%), which maximizes his opportunities to leverage elite speed\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the stolen base category. **Jose Caballero** remains a roster staple despite the optimizer dinging him for his position at the bottom of the order; his 42% SB potential provides a necessary ceiling that keeps him ahead of lower-upside depth pieces.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the ledger was bypassing **Vinnie Pasquantino** (48.79) in favor of **Josh Naylor** (55.92). While **Vinnie Pasquantino** offers consistent production, the negative platoon impact of facing Gage Jump pushed his efficiency score below our threshold for starting consideration. **Josh Naylor** retains the spot at 1B despite the uncertainty of his pending lineup position, as his raw power profile against Robert Gasser provides a higher probability of driving in runs. We are monitoring **Max Muncy** (55.33) and **Austin Riley** (56.26) closely; both face significant lineup-order penalties, and any move toward the bottom of the card would make them immediate candidates for substitution to protect our game caps.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in our heavy reliance on pending lineup data. As we await official confirmation, we are assuming standard deployment for **Josh Naylor**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Max Muncy**. Any late-breaking changes to their batting positions\u2014particularly for **Max Muncy** if he drops further down the order\u2014could collapse their daily efficiency scores. With **James Wood** still sidelined and **Mickey Moniak** inactive today, we have limited flexibility, necessitating a disciplined approach to the bench. We continue to hold **Cole Young** in reserve, who, despite a decent profile, lacks the immediate platoon advantage needed to crack the top seven.",
